3. Results
3.1. Classification using raw IMU time-series
Fig. 2A presents performance metrics of the ML models on the raw time-series, ranked by macro-F1 score. XGBoost and RF achieved the highest performance (macro-F1 = 0.87 and 0.86, respectively). SVM (RBF), MLP, LR, kNN, and DT followed with lower macro-F1 scores (0.83, 0.82, 0.80, 0.78, and 0.73, respectively). Accuracy, precision, and recall followed a similar ranking pattern (Fig. 2A; Supplementary Table 3). Class-specific F1-scores revealed clear asymmetry (PSP ≈ 0.80 vs PD ≈ 0.94).
